        "original_id": "eb0d6a82-ddc9-5754-b2cd-3768b419a798",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Columbian Iron Works and Dry Dock Company\n- Places: Baltimore, Maryland; Locust Point peninsula; Fort McHenry; Baltimore Harbor; Chesapeake Bay\n- People: William W. Morris\n- Roles: brigade commander\n- Events: War of 1812; British attack on Baltimore Harbor\n\nFacts:\n- On September 13–14, 1814, Fort McHenry in Baltimore, Maryland, successfully defended Baltimore Harbor from an attack by the British navy from the Chesapeake Bay during the War of 1812.\n- William W. Morris served as a brigade commander primarily responsible for the defense of Fort McHenry and Baltimore Harbor.\n- The Columbian Iron Works and Dry Dock Company operated from 1872 to 1899 in Baltimore, Maryland, on the Locust Point peninsula adjacent to Fort McHenry.",
